# T14 — One Slack thread is one orchestrator conversation: COMPLETE

## Files owned and changed
- `test/slack-thread.test.ts` (new): failing-first tests for thread-scoped
  orchestrator naming — exact `slack:{team}:{channel}:{thread_ts}` format,
  per-thread isolation, name stability, empty/malformed id rejection,
  `thread_ts`-vs-`ts` resolution, PR-by-default payload, GITHUB_TOKEN card
  warning, and DO stub resolution by thread name.
- `src/slack-thread.ts` (new): `buildSlackThreadName`,
  `resolveThreadTs`, `buildSlackRunPayload` (`publishPullRequest: true`,
  `source: "slack"`), `missingGithubTokenWarning` (render on the approval
  card — orchestrator.ts throws after Approve when GITHUB_TOKEN is missing),
  `getSlackThreadStub` (injectable `byName`, defaults to Agents SDK
  `getAgentByName`). Carries the required prose-boundary comment: GOAL.md's
  "do not scrape arbitrary prose" governs the child boundary; thread prose
  goes through the orchestrator LLM into structured `delegate_coding_task`.
- `.build/status/t14.done` (new): this file.

## TDD evidence
- BEFORE implement: `npx vitest run test/slack-thread.test.ts` → FAIL
  (Cannot find module '../src/slack-thread.js').
- AFTER implement: `npx vitest run test/slack-thread.test.ts` → PASS (12 passed).
- `npx eslint src/slack-thread.ts test/slack-thread.test.ts` → clean.
- `npx tsc --noEmit` → zero errors reference slack-thread files; remaining
  errors are other agents' uncommitted in-progress work (automations,
  orchestrator-result, runtime) and were left untouched.

## Commit
- "feat(slack): scope one orchestrator conversation per Slack thread"
  (exactly these 3 files, 263 insertions — verified via `git show --stat HEAD`
  immediately after committing).
- NOTE (shared-branch hazard, 2026-09-17): concurrent agents share one git
  index/branch. Mid-task, an intermediate commit with this same message
  (d3d50b8) accidentally captured another agent's staged T11 hunks
  (`sleepAfter` 10m→1m), and a later reset by a third agent dropped both that
  commit and T11's follow-up from the branch line. Neither was reverted by
  hand: the working tree still carries `sleepAfter = "1m"` (T11's change,
  intact), so tree state is correct and history noise was left alone rather
  than risking another agent's work. Lesson: on a shared branch, stage and
  commit in one command and verify `--stat` before doing anything else.

## Test command
- `npx vitest run test/slack-thread.test.ts`

